    state: "Karnataka",
    aliases: ["Chikkamagaluru"],
    tagline: "The Birthplace of Indian Coffee",
    description: "Chikmagalur, nestled in the Western Ghats, is where coffee cultivation in India genuinely began — legend credits a 17th-century Sufi saint, Baba Budan, with smuggling seven coffee beans out of Yemen and planting them in these hills, giving the nearby Baba Budangiri range its name. The district is also home to Mullayanagiri, Karnataka's highest peak, and remains one of India's most productive coffee-growing regions, with genuine working plantations open to visitors.",
