    description: "Baroda Museum & Picture Gallery, in Vadodara, was genuinely founded in 1887 by Maharaja Sayajirao Gaekwad III, an avid collector who donated his own gathered artefacts as the founding collection. The Museum building, completed in 1894 and designed by Major Mant with R.F. Chisholm, was real and deliberately modelled after London's Victoria & Albert Museum and Science Museum, in Indo-Saracenic style. The separate Picture Gallery, built 1908-14 and formally opened in 1921 after World War I, houses genuine English portraiture — including works from the schools of Joshua Reynolds and Peter Lely — across a real 28 galleries spanning Japan, China, Nepal, Europe, Tibet, Egypt, Greece and Rome, plus a gallery dedicated entirely to the Gaekwad dynasty itself.",
