    state: "Rajasthan",
    hidden: true,
    aliases: ["Amer Fort"],
    tagline: "A UNESCO Hill Fort Hiding a Palace of a Million Mirrors",
    description: "Amber Fort (also spelled Amer Fort) was commissioned in 1592 by Maharaja Man Singh I and substantially expanded under Jai Singh I (r. 1621–1667), who added the Diwan-i-Khas (Hall of Private Audience) and began the Sheesh Mahal — the fort's real showpiece, a palace of mirrors completed in 1727 whose thousands of tiny mirror fragments, imported from Belgium, were set into white marble reliefs and pietra dura floral inlay. Built in red and pale-yellow sandstone in a genuine blend of Rajput and Mughal architectural styles, the fort rises above Maota Lake on the edge of Jaipur, and in 2013 was inscribed as part of the UNESCO World Heritage \"Hill Forts of Rajasthan\" listing alongside Kumbhalgarh and four other forts.",
