    hidden: true,
    tagline: "A 10-Acre 'Sands of Night' Island, Reachable Only by Boat",
    description: "Pathiramanal — the name translates to \"Sands of Night\" — is a genuine 10-acre island in Vembanad Lake, in Alappuzha district's Muhamma panchayat, sitting between the backwaters of Thaneermukkom and Kumarakom and reachable only by boat. Historically it belonged to the Thaimattatil family before the Travancore kings leased it to a Portuguese sailor, Andrew Pereira; it passed into government ownership in 1979 after Kerala's Land Reforms Acts took effect. The island is genuinely rich in birdlife — home to 91 resident species and 50 migratory visitors, including pintail ducks, night herons, cormorants, purple herons, and bronze-winged jacanas — making it one of the backwaters' real avian hotspots. A local legend also attaches to the island's origin, holding that it rose from the lake bed where a young Brahmin once waded in for his evening ablutions — folklore alongside the island's real, documented land-tenure and ecological history.",
