    tagline: "The 'City of Spices' Where Vasco da Gama First Landed in India",
    description: "Kozhikode, historically known as Calicut, was genuinely dubbed the \"City of Spices\" for its central role in the Eastern spice trade through classical antiquity and the Middle Ages — Arab merchants traded here from as early as the 7th century, and by the medieval period the city was one of the world's principal centres for black pepper, cardamom, ginger, and cinnamon, drawing Arab and later Chinese merchants alike. Under the Zamorins, its ruling sovereigns, Kozhikode reached what's genuinely regarded as its golden age, with the Zamorins actively patronising trade and maintaining the order that let merchants from across the world do business there. That global significance turned a real historical corner on 20 May 1498, when Portuguese explorer Vasco da Gama's expedition reached the shores near Kozhikode — the first direct sea route from Europe to India, an event that irrevocably reshaped the established patterns of Indian Ocean trade and opened the era of European colonial involvement in South Asia.",
