    state: "Haryana",
    tagline: "A Sikh Gurudwara on the Ghaggar, Where Guru Gobind Singh Once Halted",
    description: "Gurudwara Nada Sahib sits on the bank of the Ghaggar river in the Shivalik foothills — a revered Sikh pilgrimage site. Guru Gobind Singh, the tenth Guru, halted here while travelling from Paonta Sahib to Anandpur Sahib after the Battle of Bhangani in 1688; a local, Nadu Shah Lubana, served him and his followers food and milk. The site remained largely obscure until Bhai Motha Singh, from a nearby village, rediscovered it and raised a platform to mark the spot. The original Manji Sahib has since been replaced by a double-storeyed domed structure with a large meeting hall, a spacious courtyard, and facilities for Guru ka Langar and pilgrim lodging — religious gatherings and community meals take place daily, with the full moon celebrated as a special occasion each month.",
