    description: "Swathed by cedar, rhododendron, fir, and Himalayan oak, the state capital of Himachal Pradesh is one of the most popular hill stations in India. Basking in the grandeur of the British era, with apparent influences in its architecture, Shimla charmed 19th-century British colonisers so thoroughly that they elevated the small township into the summer capital of an empire spanning the subcontinent. In its heyday, Shimla drew princes, merchants, diplomats, and political leaders from Afghanistan, Tibet, China, Myanmar, and beyond — several heritage buildings across the city still stand as witnesses to moments that shaped South Asian history.",
