    tagline: "The Land of Gods, on the Banks of the Beas",
    description: "Revered for its many village deities as the 'Land of Gods' (Devtas), Kullu — spread along the banks of the River Beas — is a quiet town that draws travellers, connoisseurs, photographers, filmmakers, and honeymooners year-round. As a gateway to Manali, it makes a cool escape for tired souls. Founded as the capital of Kullu in 1660, the sprawling township now serves as the administrative headquarters of the valley district — an intricate web of valleys, deep forests, gushing streams and rivers, and bountiful orchards backed by the forbidding heights of the Greater Himalayas.",
    image: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Vaishno_Devi_Temple_-_Kullu_-_Himachal_Pradesh.jpg/1280px-Vaishno_Devi_Temple_-_Kullu_-_Himachal_Pradesh.jpg",
