    description: "Amongst dizzy Himalayan heights, Kinnaur — once a forbidden land — is now a treasure trove for the daring and adventure-seekers. From the righteous greens of Sangla Valley, with its well-developed apricot and apple orchards, to the magnificent panorama of Chitkul, India's last village on the Indo-Tibet border, and from the stunning sight of Mt. Kinner Kailash — abode of Lord Shiva — seen from Kalpa, to the pristine lake at Nako village, nature's portrait is an ever-changing one here. Lying on the ancient India–Tibet trade route, ringed by the Himalayan, Zanskar, and Dhauladhar ranges, Kinnaur carries a well-conserved culture and a timeless rhythm of life.",
