    description: "Located on the banks of the Yamuna, Paonta Sahib is associated with Guru Gobind Singh, the 10th Sikh Guru, who lived here for about three years. In the closing years of the 17th century, the Guru came to the princely state of Sirmaur at the invitation of its ruler, Maidni Prakash; after surveying the area, he chose to camp by the Yamuna, and his stay here became the foundation of the town. 'Paonta' means 'a foothold' — the Gurudwara's foundations were set by Guru Gobind Singh himself, and it now overlooks the Yamuna flowing quietly by, commanding fine views of the Doon Valley and nearby hills.",
