    description: "Gulmarg, a hill station in the Pir Panjal range at 2,650m, was known as Gaurimarg before Sultan Yousuf Shah Chak renamed it in the late 16th century for the wildflower meadows that still bloom green and gold each summer. The British built a golf course and a ski club here in 1927, and the hill station has stayed genuinely serious about winter sports since — CNN has called it the \"heartland of winter sports in India,\" and it's hosted the National Winter Games three times. Its real modern centrepiece is the Gulmarg Gondola, a two-stage cable car built by the French company Pomagalski that ranks among the highest-altitude cable cars in the world, lifting skiers and sightseers alike up toward Apharwat Peak's shoulder for genuinely spectacular Himalayan views — including, on a clear day, distant Nanga Parbat.",
