    tagline: "A 5,000-Year-Old Riverside Site, Above a Fort Built for a Coronation",
    description: "Akhnoor Fort stands on the right bank of the Chenab River, about 28 km from Jammu, its towers and red-sandstone ramparts rising over the water much as they have since Raja Tej Singh began building it in 1762, with his successor Raja Dhian Singh completing the work in 1802. The fort's real historical weight comes from 1822, when Maharaja Gulab Singh was formally coroneted at the Jia Pota ghat on the riverbank just below its walls, an event genuinely tied to the founding of the princely state of Jammu and Kashmir. The site sits atop \"Manda,\" a roughly 5,000-year-old Harappan-era settlement excavated by the Archaeological Survey of India, which has protected the fort as National Monument N-JK-16 since 1982. Parts of the fort remain closed or in active restoration, and much of its interior has been lost to time and encroachment, but the river-facing view of its towers above the ghats is genuinely one of Jammu region's most striking heritage sights.",
