    state: "Jammu and Kashmir (UT)",
    tagline: "The \"Meadow of Gold\" Guarding the Old Silk Road Gateway to Ladakh",
    description: "Sonamarg sits at 2,730 metres in Ganderbal district, about 80 km northeast of Srinagar, its name — \"Meadow of Gold\" — earned honestly from the way its alpine grasslands catch the light against a backdrop of snow peaks. It has real historical weight as a former staging point on the ancient Silk Road connecting Kashmir with Tibet, and today serves the same gateway role in miniature: 15 km on at Baltal, the Zoji La pass carries the road onward toward Ladakh and Leh. Just above the town, Thajiwas Glacier is reachable by a short pony ride in summer, a popular and genuinely striking outing set in a meadow that blends straight into the ice. Sonamarg is also the standard starting point for treks into the high alpine lakes of the region — Vishansar, Krishansar, Gangabal, and Gadsar — making it as much a trekking base as a destination in its own right. The whole area is snowed in and inaccessible through winter, opening back up as the meadows bloom through the warmer months.",
    image: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Thajiwas_Park%2C_Sonamarg%2C_Jammu_and_Kashmir%2C_India.jpg/1280px-Thajiwas_Park%2C_Sonamarg%2C_Jammu_and_Kashmir%2C_India.jpg",
