    description: "Baisaran Valley is a high-altitude meadow about 5 km from Pahalgam town, sitting roughly 2,438 metres up — an open grassy bowl ringed on all sides by dense pine forest, with snow-capped Himalayan peaks rising behind the tree line, earning it the popular nickname \"mini Switzerland of Kashmir.\" There's no motorable road in; visitors reach it on foot or by a roughly hour-long pony ride from Pahalgam, arriving at a wide, flat meadow used for picnics, short walks, and photographs against the surrounding pine-and-snow backdrop. It's important that visitors know Baisaran was the site of a terror attack on 22 April 2025 that killed 26 people, one of the deadliest attacks on civilians in India in recent years, after which J&K authorities temporarily closed dozens of tourist sites across the valley and significantly increased security. Tourism to the meadow has been reported reviving through 2025 under a heavier security presence, but travellers should check current official advisories and on-the-ground conditions before visiting, and stay alert to any local guidance while there.",
