    tagline: "A 200-Metre Natural Cave With a Self-Formed, \"Unending\" Shiva Lingam",
    description: "Shiv Khori sits in Sangar village, Reasi district, roughly 140 km from Jammu, 80 km from Katra, and a 3 km walk from the Ransoo base camp — a natural limestone cave about 200 metres deep that narrows dramatically from an entrance hall spacious enough for 300 devotees down to a passage where visitors must stoop, crawl, or turn sideways to continue. At its heart sits a naturally formed Shiva lingam, said locally to be self-manifested and unending in depth, alongside natural rock formations that devotees read as images of Parvati, Ganesha, and Nandi; the cave roof carries snake-like mineral formations from which water trickles directly onto the lingam. Pilgrim numbers have grown genuinely dramatically, passing 300,000 by 2005 and climbing toward the millions in the years since, with the biggest crowds arriving for Maha Shivratri each February or early March.",
