    id: "khardung-la",
    name: "Khardung La",
    state: "Ladakh (UT)",
    tagline: "A Former Silk Road Caravan Pass, 40km North of Leh",
    description: "Khardung La sits about 40 km north of Leh on the Ladakh Range, its actual elevation of 5,359 metres genuinely impressive on its own — though roadside signage has long claimed 5,602 metres and billed it as \"the world's third highest motorable pass,\" a claim that doesn't hold up and is worth knowing before you repeat it. The pass carries real history: it lay on a major caravan route to Kashgar in Central Asia, with some 10,000 horses and camels crossing it annually in trade, wool, silk, and spices moving south while cotton, indigo, and opium moved north, and it even saw an attempted wartime supply route to China during WWII. The Border Roads Organisation built the current motorable road in 1976, and it remains a vital supply artery for the Indian Army toward the Siachen Glacier as much as a high-altitude tourist draw, connecting Leh's Indus Valley to the Shyok Valley and Nubra beyond.",
