    description: "Fotu La, at 4,108 metres in the Zanskar Range, is the highest point on the entire Srinagar–Leh Highway — genuinely higher than the more famous Zoji La, though far less visited. Reached on the Kargil–Leh leg of the 434 km highway, typically covered over two days with an overnight halt at Kargil, it's one of two major passes between Leh and Kargil alongside Namika La, and marks the point where the road begins its descent toward Lamayuru's dramatic \"moonland\" landscape. The pass itself is a genuinely striking stop: a winding ribbon of road cutting through bare, folded mountains, with prayer flags marking the summit and, on clear days, views stretching across the Zanskar range's snow-streaked peaks.",
