    id: "chadar-trek",
    name: "Chadar Trek",
    state: "Ladakh (UT)",
    tagline: "A 105km Winter Walk Across the Zanskar River's Frozen Ice Sheet",
    description: "The Chadar Trek follows the frozen Zanskar River through the Zanskar Gorge, where near-vertical cliffs rise up to 600 metres and the canyon narrows to as little as 5 metres in places — a genuinely dramatic winter route that, for the Zanskari people, was traditionally the only way in or out of their valley during the harsh winter months when mountain passes closed entirely. \"Chadar\" means sheet or blanket, referring to the ice sheet itself, which forms thick enough to walk on only from January to February, when temperatures along the gorge regularly drop to -30°C or lower. The classic route runs roughly 105 km from Chilling to Naerak (a frozen waterfall) over about 9 days, with a longer variant continuing all the way to Padum over some 14 days; Zanskari porters traditionally haul goods and gear on wooden sleds across the ice, occasionally sheltering overnight in caves along the gorge. The Border Roads Organisation's ongoing construction of the Nimmu-Padum-Darcha road, intended to give Zanskar year-round connectivity, means the trek's practical necessity is genuinely fading even as its appeal as an extreme adventure experience remains.",
    image: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Chadar-Zanskar.jpg/1280px-Chadar-Zanskar.jpg",
    heroImage: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Chadar-Zanskar.jpg/1280px-Chadar-Zanskar.jpg",
