    description: "Netarhat sits at 1,128 metres in Latehar district, earning its nickname \"Queen of Chotanagpur\" as the most-visited nature destination in western Jharkhand, about 156 km — roughly 4-5 hours — from Ranchi. Its real draw is a cluster of genuinely distinct viewpoints and natural features within a compact area: Sunrise Point and the Koel River View & Sunrise Point (3 km away) for the plateau's famous dawn light, Magnolia Sunset Point 10 km away for evenings, and the Upper and Lower Ghaghri waterfalls for a change of pace from the viewpoints. A British-era Chalet House survives as a reminder of the hill station's colonial-era origins as a summer retreat. The clearest, most reliable sunrise and sunset views come November through February, and the wider October-to-March window keeps the plateau cool and comfortable for the kind of unhurried, viewpoint-hopping visit Netarhat is built for.",
