    tagline: "Jharkhand's Famous Serpentine Road, Winding Above a Vast Reservoir",
    description: "Patratu Valley, in Ramgarh district about 35 km from Ranchi, is best known for one genuinely dramatic sight — a serpentine ghat road that switchbacks down through the Chota Nagpur Plateau's forested hills, one of the most photographed roads in eastern India. At the valley's heart sits Patratu Dam, built across the Nalkari River, its reservoir a vast, shimmering lake that mirrors the surrounding green hills and is visible in sweeping panorama from several viewpoints along the descent. The combination of the winding road itself, the reservoir view, and the forested slopes around it makes this as much a scenic drive as a single destination — a place many visitors experience from a car window as much as on foot, though roadside viewpoints let you stop and take in the full sweep of the valley.",
