    tagline: "The Santhal Spring Festival of Flowers, Marking the Tribal New Year",
    description: "Baha Parab — 'baha' meaning flower in Santali — is one of the most important festivals of the Santhal people, celebrated in the spring month of Falgun when sal, mahua, mango, and palash trees burst into fresh leaves, flowers, and fruit. A genuine festival of nature worship and renewal, it marks the tribal new year, with communities gathering at the sacred grove (jaher than) for rituals led by the village priest before erupting into exuberant collective dance — women in bright red-and-green bordered saris moving in linked-arm rows to the driving rhythm of tamak and tumdak drums, men playing and dancing alongside, all beneath the sal trees in their spring bloom. Celebrated across the Santhal Pargana region and wherever Santhal communities live, Baha Parab offers visitors a genuinely vivid, joyful window into one of Jharkhand's richest living tribal traditions.",
