    tagline: "A Towering Seaside Shiva Statue on the Konkan Coast",
    description: "Murudeshwara, on a headland of Kanduka Hill jutting into the Arabian Sea in Uttara Kannada district, is one of Karnataka's most striking convergences of myth, architecture, and coastline. Its centrepiece is a 123-foot statue of a seated Lord Shiva — among the tallest Shiva statues in the world — gazing out over the sea, behind which rises the 20-storey Raja Gopuram (around 249 feet), painted white and gold, with a lift carrying visitors to a panoramic viewpoint over the temple, town, and open ocean. The temple enshrines a part of the Atmalinga tied to the Ramayana legend of Ravana, Ganesha, and the scattered linga (a story also linked to nearby Gokarna), and the Bhukailasa Cave Museum beneath the great statue brings that myth to life with life-sized sculptures. Beyond the pilgrimage draw, Murudeshwar Beach offers calm sunsets right beside the temple, while the waters off nearby Netrani Island rank among India's finest scuba-diving sites — all within about a kilometre of each other.",
