    tagline: "A Misty Chikkamagaluru Hill Retreat of Gardens, Peaks, and Waterfalls",
    description: "Kemmanagundi (also spelt Kemmangundi) is a small hill station at about 1,434 m in Chikkamagaluru district, once developed as a summer retreat for the Wodeyars of Mysuru — hence the sunset-facing \"Raj Bhavan\" viewpoint at its heart. It is known for its terraced ornamental gardens and for the sweep of Western Ghats scenery around it: Z Point, reached by a short trek, gives one of the finest ridge-and-valley panoramas in the region, while Shanti Falls lies along the same trail. Nearby, Hebbe Falls drops in two stages through coffee-estate forest and is reached by a rough 4x4 jeep ride or a long walk, and Kalhatti Falls tumbles over elephant-shaped rocks past a small temple about 10 km away. The area is a base for peaks and jungle trails, with Mullayanagiri, Bhadra Wildlife Sanctuary, and Ayyana Kere all within reach.",
