    description: "Nagara, a quiet village in Hosanagara taluk of Shivamogga district, was once Bidanur (also Bednore, later Hyder Nagar) — the final capital of the Keladi Nayaka dynasty, who moved their seat here in 1640. Its 17th-century hill fort has been left almost entirely to nature: stone ramparts, a circular watchtower-bastion, and terraced defences rise out of grassy slopes and dissolve into the dense Malnad canopy, with valleys, lakes, and backwaters all around. Below and nearby lie the ruins of the Shivappa Nayaka palace and the stepped Devagange ponds. Maintained by the Archaeological Survey of India and free to enter, Nagara is a raw, uncrowded heritage site best explored on foot over a few hours, especially atmospheric in the monsoon when the hills turn brilliant green.",
