    description: "Maravanthe, on the coast between Kundapura and Bhatkal, is one of Karnataka's most photographed beach drives: for a few kilometres the NH66 highway runs on a narrow strip of land with the open Arabian Sea breaking on one side and the calm Souparnika River flowing quietly on the other. The name is said to mean \"sunrise on the west coast\" in Kannada. The beach itself is a long, largely unspoilt stretch of sand, best at sunset, and the contrast of surf, road, river, and hills makes even a passing drive memorable. Nearby lie the ancient Koteshwara Shiva temple, the Kavala (Kodachadri-side) caves, and the temple town of Udupi, while the riverbanks draw migratory birds in season. Swimming is not advised in the rough monsoon months (June–September).",
