    tagline: "The World's Highest Tea Plantation, Reached by Jeep Above Munnar",
    description: "Kolukkumalai, on the Kerala–Tamil Nadu ridge above Munnar in Idukki district, is generally described as the highest tea estate in the world, its bushes climbing to around 7,900 feet on steep, wind-scoured slopes. The estate still runs a 1930s tea factory that processes leaf entirely by the old orthodox method — withering, rolling, oxidising, and sorting on original British-era machinery driven by belts and pulleys — and visitors can follow the whole process and taste the results. The only way up is a slow, jolting jeep ride of roughly 90 minutes on a rough track from Suryanelli, near Munnar, and most people start before dawn to reach the Kolukkumalai viewpoint for sunrise, when the sun lifts over the Western Ghats and a sea of cloud fills the valleys below. Weather is fickle and cold at the top even in summer.",
