    id: "malampuzha-dam-garden",
    name: "Malampuzha Dam & Garden",
    state: "Kerala",
    tagline: "Kerala's Largest Reservoir, a Nek Chand Rock Garden, and a Ropeway Under the Ghats",
    description: "Malampuzha, about 10 km from Palakkad town, pairs Kerala's largest reservoir with a cluster of family attractions laid out below the wall of the Western Ghats. The dam, completed in 1955 across the Malampuzha river (a tributary of the Bharathapuzha, or Nila), is a combination earthen-and-masonry structure supplying irrigation and drinking water to Palakkad district. Below it spread landscaped gardens with fountains, a large rose garden, boating, a freshwater aquarium and (separately ticketed) snake park, and an aerial ropeway that carries small cable cars high over the gardens. Malampuzha's most distinctive feature is its rock garden, built by the Padma Shri artist Nek Chand — his second such project after Chandigarh — from broken bangles, tiles, tins, and other discarded material, opened in 1996. There is also the well-known reclining \"Yakshi\" sculpture by Kanayi Kunhiraman. Some sections (the rock garden in particular) have periodically been closed for renovation, so check current status before a special trip.",
    image: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Malampuzha_dam_Garden_mountains_Kerala_Jul21_D72_20292.jpg/1280px-Malampuzha_dam_Garden_mountains_Kerala_Jul21_D72_20292.jpg",
