    description: "Poovar lies at the far southern tip of Thiruvananthapuram district, about 35 km from the city, where the Neyyar river spreads into a lagoon and then breaks through a long golden-sand bar to reach the Arabian Sea. That sandbar — often called the \"Golden Island\" — is reached only by boat, which keeps it quiet and uncrowded: on one side the calm estuary and mangroves, on the other the open surf. The usual way to experience Poovar is a backwater boat cruise from the jetty, threading past mangrove tunnels, riverside churches, and the moored floating cottages of the resorts, with kingfishers, herons, brahminy kites, and cormorants along the banks. Sunrise and sunset over the sandbar are the highlights. Kovalam, Vizhinjam harbour, and the Azhimala Siva temple are all a short drive north.",
