    id: "thenmala-ecotourism",
    name: "Thenmala Ecotourism",
    state: "Kerala",
    tagline: "India's First Planned Ecotourism Site — 'Honey Hill' in the Western Ghats",
    description: "Thenmala, whose name means \"Honey Hill\" in Malayalam, in the forests of Kollam district is billed as India's first planned ecotourism destination, laid out in themed zones on the edge of the Shendurney Wildlife Sanctuary along the Kollam–Shencottah road. The Leisure Zone, beside the Thenmala (Parappar) Dam reservoir on the Kallada river, has landscaped gardens, a musical dancing fountain with an evening light-and-sound show, and boating on the reservoir. The Adventure Zone offers mountain biking, rock climbing, rappelling and river-crossing, plus a canopy walkway and forest trails for hiking and birdwatching. The Culture Zone has an amphitheatre and sculpture garden, and there is a butterfly safari park and a deer rehabilitation area nearby. The surrounding sanctuary is home to elephants, leopards, and rich birdlife, and the tall Palaruvi Falls is a short drive away. It is an easy road-and-rail stop, with its own small railway station.",
    image: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Reservoir_of_Thenmala_Dam%2C_Kollam.jpg/1280px-Reservoir_of_Thenmala_Dam%2C_Kollam.jpg",
