    tagline: "A Firm Golden Strand You Can Drive Along — the Longest Drive-in Beach in Asia",
    description: "Muzhappilangad, about 7 km south of Thalassery in Kannur district, is Kerala's longest beach and the best known drive-in beach in Asia: for roughly 4 km the sand is firm and flat enough to drive a car or ride a motorbike straight along the shore. A line of low black rocks offshore breaks the ocean swell, so the water close in is unusually calm and shallow — safer for a paddle than most open Malabar beaches — and those rocks also draw migratory shorebirds (terns, gulls, sandpipers) in winter. At low tide you can walk across to green Dharmadam Island just offshore. The beach hosts parasailing, microlight flights, and power-boat and catamaran rides, and every April the Muzhappilangad Beach Festival fills the sand with car and bike stunts and cultural programmes. It has featured on international lists of the world's best coastal drives.",
