    state: "Kerala",
    tagline: "A Quiet Cluster of Canal-Laced Islets Where the Kallada River Meets Ashtamudi Lake",
    description: "Munroe Island (Munrothuruthu) is a group of small, low-lying islets in Kollam district, at the confluence of the Kallada river and Ashtamudi Lake, named after Colonel John Munro, a British Resident of old Travancore. Life here runs on water: a dense web of narrow canals, lagoons, and channels threads between coconut groves, paddy plots, and tile-roofed houses, and the classic way to see it is a slow canoe or small country-boat tour that ducks under low footbridges into channels too tight for the big backwater boats. Villagers still make coir from soaked coconut husk, farm prawns and fish in the shallow fields, and go about daily life along the banks, while kingfishers, herons, and egrets work the water. It is an unhurried, homestay-style destination — cycling, birdwatching, and canal cruises rather than resorts — and one of the calmest corners of the Kerala backwaters.",
    image: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/House_Canal_Munroe_Island_Kerala_Mar22_A7C_01448.jpg/1280px-House_Canal_Munroe_Island_Kerala_Mar22_A7C_01448.jpg",
