    tagline: "Karnataka's Highest Peak, in the Grassy Baba Budan Range Above Chikmagalur",
    description: "Mullayanagiri (Mullayyanagiri) is the highest peak in Karnataka, rising to about 1,930 metres (roughly 6,317 ft) in the Baba Budangiri range near Chikmagalur, and is often described as the highest point between the Himalayas and the Nilgiris. Its upper slopes are rolling shola grassland cut by misty cliffs and cool wind, with a small Sri Mullappa Swamy shrine and a communications tower at the very top. A narrow, steep road climbs most of the way; from the road-head a flight of about 400–500 steps leads to the summit, and there are longer, more satisfying trekking routes across the ridge from Sarpadhari and Baba Budangiri. Sunrise from the top, above a sea of cloud filling the valleys, is the classic experience. It pairs with the nearby Baba Budan Giri cave shrine, Kemmangundi, and the coffee estates of Chikmagalur.",
