    description: "Kudremukh — Kannada for \"horse face,\" the shape the main peak takes from the right angle — is a mountain range and one of Karnataka's classic treks, in Chikkamagaluru district within the Western Ghats. It is the core of Kudremukh National Park, a UNESCO-recognised biodiversity area of shola forest, tall wet grassland, and countless streams; the peak itself, at around 1,894 m, is the state's second highest after Mullayanagiri. The trek to the summit runs roughly 9–10 km each way from the Mullodi/Balagal side, climbing over open rolling downs with long views, and it needs a Forest Department permit and a compulsory guide, with entry limited each day. The park also holds Hanuman Gundi (Soojidhara) falls, the Lakya dam, and — a scar it is still recovering from — a decommissioned open-cast iron-ore mine. Rain and mist are near-constant on the higher slopes; the drier winter months give the clearest walking.",
