    state: "Karnataka",
    tagline: "The Second Keladi Nayaka Capital and Its Grand 16th-Century Shiva Temple",
    description: "Ikkeri, a village about 6 km from Sagara in Shivamogga district, was the second capital of the Keladi (Ikkeri) Nayakas, who shifted here from nearby Keladi in the 16th century as their power grew across the Malnad and coast. Almost nothing of the fortified city survives, but its great temple does: the Aghoreshwara Temple, a large stone shrine to Shiva built in a distinctive Nayaka style that blends Dravidian, Hoysala, and its own local idiom. It stands on a raised platform in a garden, its outer walls and pillars carved with deities and scrollwork, a pillared open mantapa in front guarded by a pair of massive stone elephants, and a separate Nandi pavilion. Quiet and uncrowded, Ikkeri is almost always visited together with the Rameshwara Temple and museum at Keladi, a short drive away.",
