    description: "Malayattoor, on the Periyar river in Ernakulam district near Angamaly, is one of Kerala's most important Christian pilgrimage centres. Tradition holds that St Thomas the Apostle, who is believed to have reached the Malabar coast at Muziris (Kodungallur) in AD 52, came here, climbed the hill to escape hostile locals, and prayed at a rock — leaving marks devotees revere as his footprints and knee-prints. The hilltop, Kurisumudy or \"Hill of the Cross\", stands about 1,269 ft high; a replica golden cross marks the spot, and there is a well said to have healing water and the ruins of an old chapel. The Vatican has designated the Malayattoor church an International Shrine. The climb is roughly 3 km and takes about 1 to 1.5 hours, past 14 stations of the cross. During Malayattoor Perunnal — on the Sunday after Easter — hundreds of thousands of pilgrims stream up the hill, many carrying wooden crosses.",
