    tagline: "The Chalakudy River Racing Over Rock, in Hornbill Country Near Athirappilly",
    description: "Vazhachal Falls lies on the Chalakudy river about 5 km upstream of Athirappilly, in the Sholayar range of the Western Ghats in Thrissur district. Where Athirappilly drops in a broad vertical curtain, Vazhachal is different in character: the river fans out and rushes noisily over a long bed of rock and boulders, framed by dense forest and riverside bamboo. The Vazhachal forest along this stretch is one of the last places in the Western Ghats where all four of South India's larger hornbill species occur together, and the river supports rare riparian trees; the area is home to the Kadar tribal community. Viewing is from a fenced area and stone benches set back from the water — the rocks are notoriously slippery and the current strong, so getting into the river is not allowed. It is managed by the Forest Department, open roughly 8:00 AM to 6:00 PM, and is at its most powerful in the monsoon and immediately after (June–October), when the road in from Athirappilly is also at its greenest.",
