    tagline: "Three Forest Waterfalls on the Chalippuzha, in a Valley Named for Its Spray",
    description: "Thusharagiri — \"the snow-capped mountain\", for the fine mist thrown up by the water — is a set of three waterfalls in the Western Ghats near Kodencheri, about 50 km east of Kozhikode. Two hill streams meet here to form the Chalippuzha river, which then breaks into the three falls: Erattumukku, the main one, drops about 75 m; Thenpara and Mazhavil Chattom (\"rainbow fall\") lie further up. The first fall and its pool are an easy walk from the road, through rubber and spice plantations; reaching the upper two means a moderately hard trek of a few kilometres through forest, and a longer trail continues over the ridge toward Vythiri in Wayanad. The area is managed by the Forest Department, and besides trekking it is used for rock climbing and rappelling. The pool at the lower fall is a popular spot for a dip, but the rocks are slippery and the current can be strong; the falls are fullest just after the monsoon.",
