    tagline: "The World's Largest Bird Sculpture, on a Hilltop Reached by Kerala's Only Cable Car",
    description: "Jatayu Earth's Center (Jatayu Nature Park) sits on Jatayupara, a rock hill at Chadayamangalam in Kollam district, right on the Main Central Road roughly midway between Kollam and Thiruvananthapuram. Spread over about 65 acres across four hills, it is built around a colossal sculpture of Jatayu — the mythical bird of the Ramayana that fought Ravana as he carried off Sita and fell wounded on this rock. Designed by the sculptor and filmmaker Rajiv Anchal, the figure is roughly 200 ft long, 150 ft wide and 70 ft high, said to be the largest bird sculpture in the world; inside it are a museum and a 6D theatre. The hilltop, at about 350 m, is reached on foot or by a cable car — the only one in Kerala. The site also has an adventure zone (rope courses, rappelling, climbing, zip lines, paintball, archery), a helipad joyride, an Ayurveda cave centre and eateries. It is a modern, ticketed attraction rather than a heritage site, and a popular half-day stop off the highway. Opening is generally 10:00 AM to 5:00 PM.",
