    description: "Ranipuram, once known as Madathumala, is a hill area at about 750 m in the Vellarikundu part of Kasaragod district, in Kerala's far north. Its forests run straight into the Coorg (Kodagu) hills of Karnataka, and it is often called the \"Ooty of Kerala\" for its cool air and open country. The draw is a trek: from the base at Panathady a path of roughly 2 km climbs through monsoon and evergreen shola forest before opening onto broad rolling grasslands with long views over ridge after ridge of the Western Ghats. The mosaic of grass savannah and shola shelters wild elephant herds — sightings are common — along with leopards, wild dogs, deer, wild boar, Malabar giant squirrels, and hornbills. It is managed by the Forest Department as an eco-tourism trek, done with a guide, usually starting in the morning. There are a few cottages at Panathady; jeeps and buses run there from Kanhangad.",
