    description: "Gavi is a small settlement and eco-tourism zone run by the Kerala Forest Development Corporation (KFDC), high in the Western Ghats on the edge of the Periyar Tiger Reserve, near the Idukki–Pathanamthitta boundary and the Kerala–Tamil Nadu border. Getting there is part of it: a roughly two-hour jeep ride from Kumily/Vandiperiyar through cardamom estates, grasslands, sholas and gushing streams, with an entry pass collected at the Vallakkadavu forest check post. Around the hamlet are the Gavi and Kochu Pampa lakes, cardamom plantations tended by settler families, and thick forest. It is one of Kerala's best birding spots — well over 260 species, including the great pied hornbill — and holds Nilgiri langur, lion-tailed macaque, sambar, elephant herds and, near Kochu Pampa, the endangered Nilgiri tahr. KFDC packages cover it: a day trip (about 8:00 AM–4:30 PM) with a jeep tour, guided trek and lake boating, or an overnight stay in the Green Mansion eco-lodge overlooking Gavi Lake, in tree huts, or in jungle tents, with local tribal community members as guides and cooks. Advance booking with KFDC is needed.",
