    description: "Ilaveezhapoonchira is a high grassland valley near Melukavu in eastern Kottayam district, ringed by three hills — Mankunnu, Kodiyathur Mala and Thonippara — each rising to around 3,200 ft. The name means roughly \"the pond of flowers where leaves do not fall\": in the monsoon, water gathers in the hollow between the hills to form a broad seasonal lake, which dries away by peak summer. The rest of the year it is open, rolling grassland cut by rivulets, with huge views — on a clear day you can pick out six neighbouring districts and the Malankara reservoir winding through the valleys below. It is one of Kottayam's favourite trekking and sunrise/sunset spots, with the reflective rock face of Kannadipara nearby and the viewpoint of Illikkal Kallu and the Kazhukankulimali waterfall not far off. There are almost no facilities on the hills themselves; a DTPC rest house nearby is the usual base.",
