    id: "kumbalangi",
    name: "Kumbalangi",
    state: "Kerala",
    tagline: "India's First Model Tourism Village — Chinese Nets, Backwaters and Working Village Life Near Kochi",
    description: "Kumbalangi is a cluster of small islands in the backwaters on the southern edge of Kochi, in Ernakulam district, about 15 km from the city. In 2003 it was developed as India's first designated model tourism village — a project to show visitors a real, working coastal village rather than a resort. The waters around it are lined with Chinese fishing nets (well over a hundred), and daily life runs on fishing, prawn and crab farming, pokkali paddy grown in the same fields the water floods, toddy tapping, and the making of coir, nets, brooms and baskets — much of which visitors can watch or try, staying in village homestays. Canoe rides thread the mangrove-fringed channels. In the summer months the backwater sometimes lights up with bioluminescence, which locals call kavaru. It is a quiet, low-key half-day or overnight from Kochi, popular for sunset over the nets.",
    image: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Sun_set_and_china_net_-_Flickr_-_k_r_ranjith.jpg/1280px-Sun_set_and_china_net_-_Flickr_-_k_r_ranjith.jpg",
