    description: "Vellayani Lake — Vellayani Kayal — is the largest freshwater lake in Thiruvananthapuram district, a broad green sheet of water spread over several square kilometres about 10 km from the city and only a short way inland from Kovalam. It is fringed by paddy, coconut groves and low wooded rises, with lotus and water-lily beds in the shallows, and it supplies drinking water and irrigation to the area; the Kerala Agricultural University's college of agriculture sits on its bank. It is an unhurried spot for a canoe or boat ride, for birdwatching along the bunds, and for sunrise and sunset. On the shore stands a roughly 700-year-old Devi (Kali) temple, known for the Kaliyoottu Mahotsavam, a large ritual-theatre festival held once every three years. Vellayani is an easy add-on to a Kovalam stay rather than a headline sight.",
