    id: "nileshwaram",
    name: "Nileshwaram (Nileshwar)",
    state: "Kerala",
    tagline: "North Kerala's Old Cultural Capital — Theyyam, Kavus, a Folklore Palace and the Kavvayi Backwaters",
    description: "Nileshwaram — Nileshwar — is a town about 40 km south of Kasaragod town, on the estuary where the Nileshwaram river meets the Kavvayi backwaters. It was long the cultural capital of the district: the Nileshwar Rajas, who moved here from Kozhikode roughly 600 years ago, made it a seat of learning and the arts. Their two-storey Kerala-style palace, with fine woodwork, now houses a folklore centre under the state Department of Archaeology / the Kerala Folklore Academy. The surrounding country is dense with kavus (sacred groves and shrines, including serpent groves) and temple festivals, and this is heartland for Theyyam, the vivid ritual dance-worship of north Malabar, performed through the winter season. Nileshwaram also has a handloom-weaving tradition, small beaches, and easy access to the Kavvayi–Valiyaparamba backwaters just to its south.",
    image: "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Nileshwar_palace_building_-May_2023.jpg/1280px-Nileshwar_palace_building_-May_2023.jpg",
