    description: "The Kateel Sri Durga Parameshwari Temple stands on a small islet in the middle of the Nandini river, about 29 km northeast of Mangaluru in Dakshina Kannada, reached by a short footbridge from the bank. It is one of coastal Karnataka's most visited goddess shrines. Its legend ties the site to Arunasura, a demon defeated when the goddess took the form of a swarm of bees (Bhramari); the deity is worshipped here as Durga Parameshwari. Kateel is also a centre of Yakshagana, the all-night dance-drama of the region: the temple runs several Yakshagana melas (troupes), performing through the season (roughly November to May) as offerings fulfilled by devotees, and touring villages the rest of the year. The setting — water on all sides, forested banks, a small weir upstream — is as much the appeal as the temple itself. Entry is free; a dress code applies in the inner areas.",
