    description: "Sagara (Sagar) is a compact town in the Malnad hills of Shivamogga district, on the banks of the Varada river in the Western Ghats. It is best known as the natural base for the surrounding sights: Jog Falls is about 30 km away, the Keladi and Ikkeri temples of the Keladi Nayakas are a short drive south, and the Sharavathi backwaters and the island shrine of Sigandur (reached by a vehicle ferry from Holebagilu) lie to the west. In the town itself, the Shri Marikamba Temple — its tall, brightly painted tiered tower a landmark on the main street — is dedicated to a fierce form of the goddess; every three years, in February or March, it hosts the nine-day Marikamba Jatre, one of the largest temple fairs in Karnataka. The old Ganapati Kere (city tank) and the Malnad's areca and spice country add to the setting. Sagara is a stopover and a hub rather than a headline sight in its own right.",
