    description: "Bangaram is a tiny, teardrop-shaped island of about 120 acres near Agatti and Kavaratti, and the only uninhabited island in Lakshadweep run as a resort. It shares a single large lagoon with the smaller islands of Thinnakara and Parali, so short boat hops reach empty sandbars and snorkelling spots. The reef around Bangaram is rich — turtles, rays, reef sharks and, on the drop-offs, bigger pelagic fish — and there is a dive operation on the island. At night, phosphorescent plankton washed up on the coral sand can give the beach a faint bluish glow. Bangaram is also the one island in the Union Territory where alcohol is permitted, which (along with its isolation) is why it has long been marketed to \"discerning, exclusive\" travellers. Access is by boat or, in season, helicopter from Agatti, and, like everywhere in Lakshadweep, needs an entry permit.",
