    description: "Maheshwar is a historic town on the north bank of the Narmada in Khargone district, about 90 km from Indore and 40 km from Mandu. In the 18th century it was the capital of the Holkar queen Ahilyabai Holkar, remembered for her temple-building and public works across India; her fort (Ahilya Fort) and the Rajwada palace still stand above the river. Below them, broad sandstone ghats built in her time step down to the Narmada, lined with small carved shrines and chhatris and busy at dawn and dusk with bathers, boats and aarti; the little Baneshwar temple sits on a rock in the river, aligned, it is said, with the earth's axis by local tradition. Maheshwar has been a handloom-weaving centre for centuries and is the home of the fine cotton-and-silk Maheshwari saree — the Rehwa Society, based in the fort, keeps the craft going and welcomes visitors. It is an easy, atmospheric stop between Indore, Mandu and Omkareshwar, best October–March.",
